      "id": "many",
      "name": "Many eyes",
      "description": "Two copies, and the neck is crowded with them - most of the lattice carries an eye. Each is built from one cell of a single scatter, drawn four times at shrinking radius: a darker socket, the white, the iris and the pupil, concentric because they are the same cell rather than because anything lined them up. The iris colour is the horse's own and travels with the copy, so a line of these breeds an eye colour the way an ordinary line breeds a coat.",
